proof.text:
Expand $\rho_q;\gamma_c$ at $K$. Naturality of $\kappa_{r_d,q}$ at $t_{c,K}$ moves this map through the compositor. Associativity in [lem-weil-derived-direct-image-composition] says
$$(\kappa_{r_d,q}R_{j_c});\kappa_{r_c,j_c}
=(R_{r_d}\kappa_{q,j_c});\kappa_{r_d,j_d},$$
since $r_dq=r_c$ and $qj_c=j_d$. Functoriality and this identity therefore give
$$\begin{aligned}
\rho_{q,K};\gamma_{c,K}
&=R_{r_d}\bigl(\eta_{q,J_dK};R_q(b_{q,K});R_q(t_{c,K});\kappa_{q,j_c,K}\bigr);\kappa_{r_d,j_d,K}\\
&=R_{r_d}(t_{d,K});\kappa_{r_d,j_d,K}=\gamma_{d,K}.
\end{aligned}$$
The middle equality is the preceding transpose calculation. Naturality of every factor upgrades the componentwise equation to the required equality.
